    "code": "KE",
    "notes": "Payroll statutory structure and values for Kenyan companies (docs/modules/payroll.md, PAY-07, PAY-08, PAY-20, PAY-21). Each period has a status (ResearchStatus): 'researched' values come from public research (docs/country-packs-research-2026-10.md) with their confidence (high or medium; a period takes the lowest of its values), research date and sources; they are used, and every run that uses one records it and shows the 'from public research' notice until the owner confirms the value through a pack release (ADM-04). A value that is null is 'rate needed' and blocks payroll runs; a value that is absent does not apply. Low-confidence research is never entered. Every money figure is per month in minor units of the pack currency (KES cents) as a digit string; rates are percentages as strings ('12.5' = 12.5 %). effective_from 2026-01-01 is the date this pack's data starts, not the date any law took effect (the NSSF year 3 period ends on 2026-01-31; year 4 starts on 2026-02-01). rounding is {mode: half_up|down|up, unit_minor: digits} applied once to the component's result. A deduction_limit component caps the pre-tax deductions of its category (pay items marked with that pre-tax category, plus the employee shares of the components it includes) before PAYE. Labels live in lang/{locale}/payroll.php (pack.*).",
